    "notes": "The rule of three: the date's own turnaround is the setup the trucker mirrors. Cruising under the hummed jingle; BANG (our sound), both faces fall, the car sinks onto the flat, she folds her arms as \"When the day goes wrong\" comes in; Take 4's hands-only roll insert under our NEW! burst and BREEZE label and his grin and wink on \"keep it cool, turn it round\"; he gets out, pops the trunk and pulls out a checked blanket and two bottles of pop; the blanket goes over the hood (Take 4's shot), her hand takes a mint, her frown melts and her head settles on his shoulder; Take 4's sunset wide under the announcer. The music drops out as the tow truck pulls up and both turn to look; the driver climbs down tired and sighs; without a word the hero holds out the roll; the trucker's hand takes a mint and his face softens as hers did; he sits down, rests his head on the hero's other shoulder as the sung \"Feel the Breeze!\" comes in, she opens one eye (pushed in on her face), and Take 3's packshot with our BREEZE logo and Turn your day around!. Cut by br5/edit.mjs in the media folder; every in and out point is a whole frame. Nobody speaks on camera: the only voice is the announcer (br-vo.wav), and the lyrics are sung in the jingle. The jingle's bed after its lyrics runs out before the truck, so one bar (2.146 s, measured) repeats at a bar line under the announcer duck: the jingle is two music clips with a 10 ms crossfade and the same volume keys (a bed with parts would say it as one sound, but a line heard in a bed can't carry word timings). Our sounds: bang, tyre hiss, the truck's engine and door, crickets; the driver's sigh is his take's own sound, run on under the next shot."
  },
